course: dictionary
lesson: 10031
title: Tentacles: long, bendy arms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tentacle is a long, bendy, arm-like part on some animals. Octopuses, squids, jellyfish and slugs all have them. Animals use tentacles to feel, grab, move or sting. «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles with suckers only on their wide tips, ten limbs in all.» So a tentacle is a kind of arm, but not every arm is a tentacle.
explain: Scientists are careful with these words. «An octopus has eight arms with suckers all along them, and scientists call them arms, not tentacles.» A squid has two longer tentacles as well as its eight arms. When you read about an animal, look at the name of each limb and check which kind it is.
explain: Some tentacles sting. «Box jellyfish have tentacles covered in tiny stinging cells that fire like harpoons.» Jellyfish use their tentacles to catch food. This is why people at the beach are told not to touch jellyfish, even dead ones, because the tentacles can still sting.
explain: The word can also be used in another way. «The tentacles of the gang» means the ways the gang reaches into many places, like long arms stretching out in every direction. This is figurative language: the word is used to describe something that is not really an animal's arm.
fact: A tentacle is a long, bendy, arm-like part used for feeling, grabbing, moving or stinging.
fact: «A slug has four tentacles: the top two carry eyes and the bottom two feel and smell.»
fact: «A squid has 8 arms and 2 longer tentacles, and like an octopus it has 3 hearts.»
fact: Jellyfish use tentacles to sting their prey.
fact: Scientists call an octopus's limbs arms, not tentacles.
exercise: What is a tentacle? | A bone inside the body | A hard shell that protects the body | *A long, bendy, arm-like part used for feeling, grabbing, moving or stinging | A fin used for swimming through the sea
exercise: An octopus has eight limbs with suckers. What do scientists call them? | Legs | *Arms | Fins | Tentacles
exercise: Which animal has eight arms and two longer tentacles? | A jellyfish | A slug | A starfish | *A squid
test: In «the tentacles of the gang», what does tentacles mean? | Soft pads on their feet | A secret hiding place | *The ways the gang reaches into many places | Long, bendy arms belonging to the gang members
test: Why should you not touch a dead jellyfish on the beach? | It is too heavy to lift | *Its tentacles can still sting | It will be sticky and smell bad | Dead jellyfish are always harmless to touch
exam: A slug has four tentacles. What do the top two carry? | *Eyes | Stingers | Slime | Suckers
